[15.388,"o","# Mission: fix hello world greeting (parallix-adhoc-0001)\r\n\r\n## Goal\r\nMake `hello.sh` print the correct greeting. Currently it prints `Helo, Wrld!`; it must print `Hello, \b World!`.\r\n\r\n## Why Now\r\nThe repository's only executable, `hello.sh`, is the canonical first-run output of the project and i \bt emits a misspelled greeting (`Helo, Wrld!`). This is the lowest-barrier correctness signal in the  \brepo and the harness-created task targets it directly. Fixing it removes the one visible defect stan \bding between the scaffolded repo and a clean, verifiable state.\r\n\r\n## Refinement Signals\r\n- Predicted NEL bucket: Small (0–80)\r\n- Confidence: High\r\n- Selection note: activate as-is\r\n- Main drivers: synthetic backlog task `fix-hello-world-greeting`, single-file regression of literal \b output\r\n\r\n## Scope\r\n- Edit `hello.sh` so its output is exactly `Hello, World!` followed by a single trailing newline.\r\n- Verify output with `./hello.sh` against the expected literal.\r\n- Keep the shebang and `printf`-based implementation approach.\r\n\u001b[7mmissions/parallix-adhoc-0001/MISSION.md\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
